## Model card

- **Name:** Codestral 25.08
- **Short description:** Mistral AI’s Codestral 25.08 is a specialized low-latency code model for IDE autocomplete, fill-in-the-middle (FIM), and multi-language development (256K context per metadata).
- **Provider / access:** Mistral AI (La Plateforme/API) and partners. Local metadata lists `opencode/codestral-25.08`, pricing $0.30/$0.90 per 1M, and `noFreeId`.
- **Release / knowledge:** Mistral announcement page reviewed 2026-11-10. Knowledge cutoff not explicitly stated in reviewed source.
- **IDs:** `codestral-25.08`, `Codestral 25.08`.
- **Context window:** 256,000 tokens total (8,192 max output) per local metadata.
- **Modalities:** Text and code input/output.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-10):** $0.30/$0.90 per 1M input/output tokens (Mistral AI La Plateforme/OpenRouter) per metadata.
- **Architecture:** Proprietary/specialized code model (Codestral family). Detailed architecture/parameter count not disclosed in accessible reviewed content.

### Raw benchmarks found

> SELF-EXCLUSION: I reviewed Mistral’s Codestral 25.08 announcement page, which reports product/quality improvements (e.g. +30% accepted completions, +10% retained code, 50% fewer runaway generations, +5% instruction following, +5% average MultiplE) but does not provide clearly extractable, independently verifiable standardized benchmark numerics for the methodology categories used here (SWE-bench, Terminal-Bench, GPQA, AIME, LiveCodeBench, etc.) attributable to this exact model version. To avoid unverifiable or misattributed scoring, this file is saved as `.md.excluded` (notes only; scores ignored).

